[h1]Buzzness Tycoon 0.2.2 — The Progression Update[/h1]

This update reworks how the hive grows in the mid and late game, adds new things to do on the meadow, and fixes the most requested annoyances (Alt-Tab, hello).

[h2]Upgrades that keep going[/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]Repeatable upgrades[/b] — many tree nodes can now be bought again and again to level up. Owned nodes show their level and the price of the next one.
[*] [b]Honey x16 and x32[/b] are in, plus [b]Honey Boost[/b]: +25% honey per level, no cap.
[*] [b]Grow Speed, Grid Ring and Storage[/b] are each a single node you keep leveling instead of three separate ones. Existing saves convert automatically.
[*] [b]Gardener bees[/b] got their own line: [b]Green Thumb[/b] (plant more often) and [b]Composting[/b] (see below).
[/list]

[h2]Aura, reworked[/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]Lab: Aura[/b] is now visible — pulsing rings spread from your hive across the meadow.
[*] Flowers [b]inside the rings[/b] give bonus pollen. Level [b]Lab: Aura[/b] to raise the bonus and [b]Aura Reach[/b] to widen the rings.
[*] Burst and Bloom have been retired; Instant Grow and Aura carry the late game.
[/list]

[h2]Life (and death) on the meadow[/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]Flowers can rot.[/b] When an old flower withers it may stay behind, grey and useless, blocking its tile. Click it to clear the spot — or buy [b]Composting[/b] and let your gardeners tidy up as they fly.
[*] [b]Plant what you want:[/b] click an empty tile to choose a Dandelion, Rose or Tulip (handy for lining up 2x2 Super Flowers).
[*] [b]Bigger meadows grow more flowers.[/b] Flower growth now scales with your grid size, so expanding actually raises your income.
[*] [b]Storage is real now:[/b] honey stops at your storage cap, shown on the HUD with a meter. Spend it or upgrade Storage!
[/list]

[h2]Shop & interface[/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]Buy bees in bulk[/b] — x1 / x10 / x25 buttons (or Shift-click).
[*] Cleaner HUD: honey, capacity, multiplier and income on one line.
[*] Aura and Instant Grow status live in the side panel with icons.
[*] The upgrade tree fits the window at any UI scale, and scrolls if it still can't.
[*] Title screen: [b]Continue[/b] / [b]New Game[/b].
[/list]

[h2]Options & fixes[/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]New Options screen[/b] (title screen and pause menu): window mode, language, volume, UI scale.
[*] [b]Alt-Tab works[/b] — the game now runs as a borderless window by default. Prefer exclusive fullscreen? It's in Options.
[*] Fixed clicks landing away from the cursor on Windows with display scaling (125% / 150%).
[*] Old saves load fine; your progress carries over.
[/list]

Thanks for playing — and for the feedback. Keep it coming!
